From 0977fd616a60d1e591905ac91b902d1e177c1c79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A9 project <dmayala@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:37:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm/a9_eink: frame pacing: prepare the update before
 power-up, drive-gap counters, nice -10

Boot 12 E5c: late +4, vbl_skips +6, max_gap 47.8 ms, after an all-zero
frame (the interlock never fired). The update's set-up (request builder,
step arrays, conditioning over 1.36 M pixels, pack) ran between the init
flash and the update's first frame, with HV on, on the one boot CPU.

- Engine: a9e_begin() split into a9e_prepare() (everything that does not
  depend on the temperature bin) and a9e_start(bin); a9e_assume_white()
  and a9e_init_end() let the update be prepared on the levels the init
  flash leaves, before the flash runs. a9e_begin() == prepare + start;
  host test: identical frames, levels and previous mode.
- a9_update: a9e_prepare() now runs BEFORE the pipeline powers up; with HV
  on only the init flash and the frames remain (a9e_start is a few
  stores). An update refused after the prepare but before any frame
  (power-up, temperature, bin) restores the levels it changed (the glass
  is untouched). Dry runs keep their own save/restore. last.prep_us.
- Real updates run at nice -10 (dry runs at 0): userspace on the boot CPU
  (sampler, logger, shells) cannot delay a frame; the worker sleeps in
  every commit, and the -20 kworkers (fp9929a max_on, emergency PWRUP drop)
  still preempt it.
- Transport: late_drive, vbl_skips_drive and max_gap_drive_us count only
  the gaps during which a drive frame (front not null) was on the glass:
  the gaps that add drive pulses. The totals stay.
- status line 2: " late_drive %llu vbl_skips_drive %llu max_gap_drive_us
  %u"; line 3: " prep_us %u".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
